@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title Flow: individualProvider page\nConstruct the page from a sessioned utterance — triage, scope mining to the page's members, dispatch (specialty_filter and geo in parallel), reconcile on provider_search, respond

actor "Person / Client" as P
participant "Gate\n(facade, transport only)" as GATE
participant "UniversalNavigator\n(SharedServices main)" as UN
database "Registry\n(the one live map)" as REG
database "Repository\nsessions, ledger, params" as REPO
participant "UtteranceManager\n(classify + RequestUsersRefinement)" as UM
participant "UniversalNavigatorProxy\n(FindCare satellite)" as PXY
participant "specialty_filter\n(tool)" as SF
participant "geo\n(tool: resolves free-text\ngeography incl. misspellings)" as GEO
participant "provider_search\n(tool)" as PS

P -> GATE : POST /  { session_token, head,\nparams(utterance, history) }
activate GATE
note over GATE
  The gate knows only transport: it collects the token, the HTTP
  head, and the POST/GET params, each if present, and hands them
  on. No routes of its own, verifies nothing.
end note
GATE -> UN : pass(session_token, head, params)
activate UN
deactivate GATE

== Triage: which of the five call types is this ==
UN -> REG : read the live map for this env
REG --> UN : routes, may_call, pages, required_members
UN -> UN : proof is a session_token ->\ncall_type = client_sessioned
UN -> REPO : verify token, advance nonce,\nload in-force parameters
REPO --> UN : session ok, params in force
note left of UN
  The UniversalNavigator is the only node that takes external
  traffic. It triages every arrival by its declared proof
  (one of five call types). client_sessioned here; a bad or
  missing proof is refused.
end note

== Determine the page and scope mining ==
UN -> UN : page = individualProvider\nmembers: provider_search (required),\nspecialty_filter, provider_detail,\nprovider_selection, geo
UN -> UM : classify(utterance, history)\nfragments scoped to individualProvider members
activate UM
UM --> UN : dispatch set { specialty_filter, geo, provider_search }
deactivate UM
note right of UM
  One model call: cached preamble plus the page members'
  registry fragments in, routes out. Knows no parameters,
  never waits on a tool. The assembled fragments ARE the
  classifier.
end note

== Render ledger: record what the page owes ==
UN -> REPO : record expectation = required_members\n{ provider_search } ; start render_timeout budget
note left of REPO
  Dispatch records the page's required_members as ledger
  expectations. Each completion callback closes one; the
  completeness.render_timeout_seconds budget races them.
end note

== Dispatch: specialty_filter and geo run in parallel ==
par
  UN -> PXY : dispatch specialty_filter { complaint }\n(satellite, our_signature signed out)
  PXY -> SF : relay locally (function call)
  SF --> PXY : { nucc_codes, UserRefinementRequestText }
  PXY --> UN : internal_callback { nucc_codes }\nproof: our_signature verified
else
  UN -> PXY : dispatch geo { free-text geography }\n(satellite, our_signature signed out)
  PXY -> GEO : relay locally (function call)
  GEO --> PXY : { geography resolved, or\npending_disambiguation, UserRefinementRequestText }
  PXY --> UN : internal_callback { geography }\nproof: our_signature verified
end
note over SF, PS
  Every tool output carries UserRefinementRequestText: populated =
  the tool is ASKING the user, delivered via the UM's
  RequestUsersRefinement(question); empty = the tool is answering.
  geo populates it when it returns pending_disambiguation.
end note
UN -> REPO : merge serially (deterministic);\na state conflict RAISES

alt geography resolved by geo (required input met)
  UN -> PXY : dispatch provider_search\n{ nucc_codes, geography }
  activate PXY
  PXY -> PS : relay locally (function call)
  activate PS
  PS --> PXY : { rows, total, UserRefinementRequestText }
  deactivate PS
  PXY --> UN : internal_callback { rows }\nproof: our_signature verified
  deactivate PXY
  alt required member closes within render_timeout_seconds
    UN -> REPO : close provider_search entry;\nserial merge (conflict RAISES)
    UN -> UN : page reconciled -\nrequired_members all closed
  else render_timeout budget expires first
    UN -> UN : ledger race lost -> layman on_timeout\nexplanation (instrumented, timings)
  end
else geography unresolved / ambiguous - required input unmet
  UN -> UM : RequestUsersRefinement(question)\n{ need geography, in-force, utterance }
  activate UM
  UM --> UN : one user-facing sentence (prose)
  deactivate UM
  note right of UM
    RequestUsersRefinement is a capability of the UtteranceManager,
    not a separate tool, and it has two forms on one conversational
    surface. RequestUsersRefinement(question): a dispatched tool
    authored the question (its UserRefinementRequestText) and the UM
    delivers it -- the case here. RequestUsersRefinement(): the UM's
    own LLM authors the question when classification finds no
    dispatchable route or a missing slot. No tool talks to the user
    directly; provider_search does not dispatch without geo having
    resolved geography; the page waits; the person's next utterance
    resolves geography through the same path.
  end note
end

note over UN, REPO
  Page error management, all instrumented with timings at a
  severity matching impact:
  * timeout  -> respond with the layman on_timeout explanation
  * parameter / state merge conflict -> RAISE
  * a required member that dies or never calls back -> RAISE
  Every throw ends in a UniversalNavigator; the proxy re-raises.
end note

UN -> GATE : stream the merged answer, sequenced\n(the gate owns the one stream)
activate GATE
GATE -> P : the one stream the gate writes
deactivate GATE
deactivate UN

@enduml
